#!/usr/bin/env python3
import os
from pathlib import Path
from release_meta import ROOT, version

release, _ = version()
folder = ROOT / 'dist'
from plan_build import selected_platforms
platforms = selected_platforms(os.environ.get('RELEASE_PLATFORMS', '["android","macos","windows","linux"]'))
assets = {
    'macos': ['macos-arm64.dmg', 'macos-arm64.zip'],
    'windows': ['windows-x64-setup.exe', 'windows-x64.zip'],
    'linux': ['linux-x64.deb', 'linux-x64.tar.gz'],
    'android-tv': ['android-tv-armeabi-v7a.apk', 'android-tv-arm64-v8a.apk', 'android-tv-x86_64.apk'],
    'android': ['android-armeabi-v7a.apk', 'android-arm64-v8a.apk', 'android-x86_64.apk'],
}
required = [suffix for platform in platforms for suffix in assets[platform]]
for suffix in required:
    file = folder / f'Hongguo-{release}-{suffix}'
    if not file.exists() or file.stat().st_size == 0:
        raise SystemExit(f'Missing installer: {file.name}')
signed = os.environ.get('IOS_SIGNED') == 'true'
if signed and not (folder / f'Hongguo-{release}-ios-arm64.ipa').is_file():
    raise SystemExit('Signed iOS job succeeded but IPA is missing')
ios = 'Signed IPA included; install only on devices covered by its provisioning profile.' if signed else 'iOS was not built in this run. Enable signed iOS explicitly to attach an installable IPA.'
tv = ('Android TV APKs carry a leanback launcher, a home-screen banner and no touchscreen requirement; '
      'every attached TV APK was checked against its own badging before upload.') if 'android-tv' in platforms else 'Android TV was not built in this run.'
(folder / 'iOS-signing-status.txt').write_text(ios + '\n')
notes = ROOT / 'build/release-notes.md'
notes.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
notes.write_text(f'''Native Flutter / shared Dart release {release}.

- macOS: hidden native titlebar, immersive player, scoped always-on-top, retained windows and menu bar controls.
- macOS PiP: automatic next episodes and mouse-driven auto-hiding playback controls.
- macOS online playback: turning on 后台下载 handed every video transfer to background_downloader, which ships no macOS implementation, so the import fell through to a pure-Dart isolate queue that stops at a fixed byte count on the same URL without ever raising an error or hitting a timeout. The stalled jobs kept holding both preparation slots, so later episodes never published and the player was left with a texture whose rect stays 0x0 forever -- which is what reading "the Mac app cannot load online video" actually was. Desktop now always transfers in-app over Dio and the switch only decides whether caching keeps being prepared while the window is hidden; cache pruning also reclaims the `.part` working files a killed session leaves behind, which had piled up as unusable ciphertext against the byte budget. Verified in a real macOS window against the live API on a series with nothing cached: 3 episodes prefetched, one acquired online at 12,020,592 bytes and played at 1920x1080, seek 10000 -> 10000 ms, next-episode switch in 307 ms with stages 正在排队 -> 已就绪 and no 正在下载 at all, while the same URL that stopped mid-transfer under the system lane in the recorded repro completes end to end under the Dio lane.
- Catalog: recover empty upstream responses and sign requests when required.
- Playback URL acquisition: the player endpoint started checking whether the device_id/iid pair it is sent is one the platform actually issued, and answers a per-request synthetic pair -- with its six signature headers -- by HTTP 200 and no body at all, which reached viewers as FormatException: Unexpected end of input. The app now registers one anonymous playback device per process (a ttEncrypt envelope, checked against offline vectors pinned from the reference implementation for framing, key schedule and the payload it carries), sends that identity unsigned with the player's own User-Agent, and reads the tracks the newer answer inlines instead of asking a second endpoint that has nothing to add. An answer that carries an envelope and declines the episode stops at once in the viewer's language, because repeating it changes nothing; a missing envelope still gets its bounded recoveries inside the same deadline. Verified against the live API: registration and acquisition both answered unsigned, and an episode acquired, downloaded and played at 1080x1920 in a real macOS window.
- Catalog filters on every non-TV build speak one language: 类型 is the first level of BOTH pages and carries one shared value, 题材 is the second level in a strip that stays on screen -- and so does the 类型 row above it, because the only thing a scroll folds away is the search box, the offline check and the swipe hint; a filter row that left with the header could only be changed again by scrolling all the way back to the top, which is what "the filters disappear after a long scroll up" was. Each sideways row also brings the chip its own level names back into view, by the smallest movement of that row's offset and never by asking an ancestor viewport to scroll, so a swipe that turned 类型 or a strip refilled by another type shows what it turned to instead of parking off the edge. Every group is a chip row of one height: the trigger that opened a sheet of every group at once is gone, along with its full-screen dismiss area. 推荐/最新 really change what is requested (最新 asks the catalog for online_time, the others keep the sort set in 设置), 榜单 takes the 类型 row out because rank(board) ignores it, and 题材 is bucketed per type so one empty upstream answer dirties only its own type. Each theme keeps its own entries, page cursor and scroll offset, so coming back returns the list exactly where it was left; rapid choices collapse into one request. Verified state by state from iPhone simulator frames recorded against the live API, including the frame where 类型 is changed to 漫剧 while the top is still folded away, and the handover frame whose strip now shows 全部 · 漫剧 instead of cutting it off.
- Catalog pages swipe like pages on touch and stylus, in three levels that each answer only their own question: 发现 and 分类 slide sideways into each other, each of them pages sideways through the shared 类型 (短剧/漫剧/AI 短剧), and each of those pages sideways through its own 题材 -- or through the three boards while 发现 is on 榜单. A swipe moves the level you are on, and only a pull past its last page hands the gesture one level up, so one gesture never skips a level and a mouse drag never flips a page by accident. The levels that hand over clamp instead of rubber-banding, because an out-of-range iOS bounce reports no overscroll at all and every handover counts exactly that report -- so the chain answers on iPhone as well as on Android. Every page keeps its own rows, cursor and scroll offset, and re-entering one continues where it was left instead of asking the catalog again, including a page that was swiped away while its own first request was still running; leaving a 类型 drops the 题材 picked inside it, and the 类型 both pages share stays selected on either side. Verified from iPhone simulator frames recorded against the live API, including the pull that turns 题材 while 类型 and the selected tab both stay put, and the one that hands over to the next 类型 at the end of the strip.
- Player controls: the bar under the picture was rebuilt around the two families it has to serve. Desktop gets a self-drawn full-width progress bar with a buffer layer and a hover time bubble, play/pause, ±10s, previous/next, a continuous volume slider whose mute icon remembers the last level, and 当前/总时长 read as h:mm:ss; the right cluster carries 选集、清晰度、倍速、投屏、悬浮播放 and 全屏, and a narrow window drops items in a fixed order while play, 选集, 倍速 and 全屏 never do. A click on the picture is now play/pause -- moving the mouse is what reveals the bar -- and a double-tap in the centre does the same, on the left or right third steps 10 seconds; the 收起 chevron (隐藏播放操作) is gone on every build. Touch keeps its contract (the first tap while hidden only reveals, never pauses), adds the same half-screen double-tap, a long press for temporary 2x and horizontal drag on the bar's own hot zone, and 清晰度 moves into the bar wherever it fits (wide desktop, phone landscape) so that state has one entry point instead of two. Keyboard: Space/K, J/L, arrows, ↑/↓, M, PageUp/PageDown, F, I. Verified from before/after frames in a real macOS window and on an iPhone simulator against the live API, and state by state in a widget suite that mounts the transport against a fake player for all four surfaces; the two-tap semantics are only provable there (a synthetic pointer cannot make a real double tap in a live host), and the phone's portrait seek frame and every landscape frame are still open.
- Catalog navigation: clicking a sidebar entry on a desktop host lands on the other page at once instead of sliding it over 300ms, because the click already is the whole request; the touch hosts keep the animation on the same pager, where a finger can end a drag between two pages. `Duration.zero` was not the fix -- it reaches `DrivenScrollActivity`, which asserts on it in a debug build -- so it is the package's own jump path. Measured by sampling the pager position after every click in a real macOS window: 81 samples across four clicks, none of them between two pages, against 10/9/11/11 in-flight samples with the animation switched back on in the same tree.
- Auto update: the app now asks GitHub Releases for the newest published version -- on the first frame and again on resume, at most once a day, carrying the feed's own ETag so a「没有变化」answer costs no body -- and shows what it found as a dialog whose release note scrolls inside its own box, because the published note runs past 12,000 characters. The check reads only the public API and sends no credentials; 设置 gained a 检查更新 row for a manual check and a switch for the silent one, and an offer can be ignored for that version or dismissed for now. What happens next is decided per platform: a download always lands as `.part`, is hashed, and is only renamed when its digest matches what the release said -- a missing digest stops the install instead of skipping the check -- then Windows hands the verified setup to its silent installer, macOS opens the verified `.dmg` (the sandbox stays on, so replacing the app is still the viewer's own drag), Linux hands the `.deb` to the system package manager, Android writes a PackageInstaller session for the verified APK and lets the system's own confirmation decide, and iOS, which has no self-install path, shows the release page address. TV builds do not take part at all. Verified in a real macOS window against the live feed end to end: prompt, scrolling note, manual check, a 22,547,501-byte download whose progress bar actually moved, sha256 match, the dmg handed to the system, and a second check that did not re-prompt. That run is also where five defects only a window could show were found and fixed -- the scrollbar asserting with no position attached, a 304 answering「自上次检查以来没有新版本」over an offer still standing, a transfer that never rebuilt the bar, the dialog quoting the Android APK's size on a Mac, and a re-prompt after a successful handoff. No Windows, Linux or Android device was available, so no install claim is made for those, and no frame was attached in this round.
- Discover, mouse family: the filter layers now belong to the page they answer for. 榜单 is its own destination in the sidebar rather than a strip inside 发现, the 类型/题材 rows keep their own scroll and only turn themselves, and a dropdown takes the vocabulary the catalog actually publishes for the current genre instead of a hand-written list -- so an empty upstream answer dirties one row, not the page. The vocabulary and the boards are read through the published filter API (select_items / category_dim_theme / selected_items / sub_selected_items), whose shape was pinned from four live samples rather than guessed.
- Discover, touch family: the filter row pins to the tail of the header so a long scroll no longer buries it, 排序 opens its own sheet, the multi-dimension drawer scrolls inside its anchor instead of clipping its own 完成 button, and 榜 gets an entrance that carries the picked 类型 with it.
- Player: opening 选集 now lands on the episode being watched instead of on 第 1 集, and the grid pages itself to it -- the segment that holds the current episode is the segment that is drawn.
- Playback: an answer that declines the device identity is traded for a fresh registration before the player is asked a second time, so a refused pair costs one request rather than a dead player.
- These four are proven state by state in the unit and widget suites (catalog vocabulary, ranking pages, episode reveal, network retry) and against the live samples recorded under docs/evidence/ranking-fields. No macOS-window or iPhone-simulator frame was captured for them in this round, so no on-device claim is made here; that pass belongs to the Mac acceptance step.
- Android update install: a verified APK used to open nothing on a phone that had not granted 安装未知应用. The manifest declared REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES but declared is not granted, and that permission is a settings-only special access on Android 8+, so no runtime dialog can ask for it -- the session committed, the app answered「已交给系统安装器，请在弹窗中确认安装。」and nothing ever appeared. The channel now asks the system whether it already accepts installs, hands the viewer the 未知来源设置 page when it does not, keeps the verified APK in memory rather than on disk while it waits, and completes the handoff on resume. The commit's PendingIntent is finally read too: PENDING_USER_ACTION launches the confirmation Intent the system hands over, FAILED surfaces the system's own message instead of a generic fallback, and a channel that never answers is bounded by a 60-second deadline so the dialog cannot freeze on 正在下载…. TV builds never reach this path. Proven by 7 widget tests that pin the order (never open a session before the grant) and by the Kotlin actually compiling into the debug mobile APK; no physical phone install is claimed.
- Android TV, five pages: 详情、我的、本地缓存、设置 and 下载管理 were rebuilt so every row is one reachable target with a visible ring, instead of a touch layout the D-pad walks straight past. The detail page carries its own 返回 target (an AppBar arrow the remote cannot land on is decoration), the episode grid marks and reveals the episode this device left off on, and 删除 answers its confirmation with the remote alone. 设置 and 下载管理 became one-target-per-row pages; the queue is also a 下载管理 button in the detail action line, because the phone's post-download snackbar action never takes focus and is therefore unpressable on a television.
- Detail page, 题材 words: the genre names the upstream already sends are now drawn under the header, and only a word the discover page's own 题材 row also publishes becomes an entry -- tapping it pops back to discover with that filter applied, leaving sort, scroll offset and the other dimensions untouched. A word that is not on the panel stays plain text, because the promise 「点它 = 回到发现页并带上这个筛选」 can only be kept for an id the panel actually has. The recommendation rail and the tag row now read the SAME panel (the genre the discover page is on), so 「同题材 · X」 cannot be earned by a request made against a different type.
- Detail page fixes underneath that: the merged Drama dropped `tagNames`, so every recommendation block silently degraded to 平台热门 -- the same bug the remote family had, since both pages now share one merge rule. The offline snapshot also started storing the words, so a detail page read without network still has a tag row and a same-theme block instead of neither.
- Detail page, remote family: the same 题材 words are shown as text (no fake chip, since the TV 发现页 has no consumer for a hand-off yet), the offline snapshot arrives paired with a reachable 重试刷新, and the episode grid's number and 第 a/b 页 line now take their sizes from the host -- 26/18 on a television, where the pager's own arrows are 26 and the page title 32, and the phone and desktop keep reading 16/14. A probe at 390x844 measured the narrow-screen proposal and closed it as not-a-fix: the two primary actions need 224.6pt of a 188pt column, a 110pt cover still only gives 208pt, and the title's font size does not enter that arithmetic at all -- so stacking them stays the design, not a bug.
- Also fixed here: the three retry paths on the TV detail page called `setState(() => future = _open())`, and a callback returning a Future is rejected by Flutter's assert -- the page had only ever been tested for whether the retry item existed, never for pressing it. The first test that actually pressed it caught this.
- These six are proven in the unit, widget and TV-flavor suites (+370, 1 flavor-gated skip) and against the live samples under docs/evidence; both Android flavors built as debug APKs. No television and no phone was photographed for them, so no on-device claim is made, and the tag-row hand-off's real-device reading is still open.
- Requests: a superseded catalog, detail or media request now releases its own transfer through a cancellation scope instead of racing the newer one, short and long Retry-After and empty upstream responses are recovered inside a shared deadline, and metadata / media-preparation / player-open timings are kept per stage in memory only -- no request parameters, URLs or keys are stored or uploaded. Measured on a macOS window and an iPhone simulator; no phone frame was attached in that round, so no phone claim is made.
- My library: favorites, per-episode watch history, resume playback and offline series.
- Episode downloads: select episodes and quality, manage tasks, retry and play offline.
- Background downloads across an app run: 后台下载 used to forget the difference between a pause the system caused and a pause the viewer pressed -- every task a previous run left unfinished came back asking for its own tap, and nothing moved until each row was pressed again. The queue now persists that distinction and re-queues automatically only on a host that actually owns a transfer lane outliving the process, which is a phone with 后台下载 turned on; desktop and TV keep waiting for the tap because their transfers died with the app. The re-queue starts only after the host has adopted the files the system lane finished while the app was away, so a phone does not re-download something that already completed. 下载管理 also gained 继续全部, which re-queues every paused, failed and cancelled task in one press.
- Cached dramas are one unit to delete or to refresh: 删除本剧缓存 takes a series' cached files and its unfinished queue records together, leaves a file that is still playing alone, then reads the real file list back and reports honestly how many files, how many bytes and how many records went -- and how many could not be removed. 拉取最新剧集 asks the catalog what that series has online now and queues only the episodes the shelf is missing, at the quality the shelf already uses, without re-queueing anything already waiting; 待识别视频 has no series id to ask with, so it refuses before any request goes out. The ranking board carries no drama grouping and therefore grows none of these entries.
- These three are proven in the unit and widget suites -- 18 new cases (4 restart continuation, 3 grouped delete, 5 online pull, 6 page walks for touch and remote) over a single-slot fake transfer lane, with `packages/app` reading 388 passed / 1 conditional skip / 0 failed and `flutter analyze` clean. No phone and no television was attached this round, so the real system download handoff, notification authorisation and the Wi-Fi-only constraint stay unverified on device; that pass belongs to the Mac acceptance step.
- DLNA casting on Android phones: one cast session belongs to the app rather than to the player page, so stepping away keeps the television running and a draggable floating handle brings the controls back from any page. The remote page drives the whole series: an episode sheet, previous/next, quality switching that puts the playhead back, another television taking the same episode at the same position, and an episode tail that hands on the next one when 自动续播 is on. Playback is only handed back to the phone when the viewer presses 退出投屏. Not yet verified against a physical receiver.
- Search: focusing the box drops a panel with the three most recent queries, each deletable and stored on this device only, plus upstream board picks marked new or hot; a history row runs the search and a board row opens its detail page.
- Player: swipe up or down on the picture to change episodes, touch and stylus only, with a one-time hint on first entry (gesture wording on phones, Page Up/Page Down on desktop) and boundary feedback instead of a silent no-op for keys, buttons and TV remote steps. Gesture behaviour is widget-tested; on-device verification is still open.
- Detail page: watch, download and favorite share one action row and the episode list is now a height-capped block of 3–4 rows that pages sideways (arrow keys, mouse drag or touch), so a long series no longer pushes the page downward. TV keeps the same block on a focusable rail.
- Detail recommendations: a horizontal rail under the episodes reads the upstream genre names of the current drama and shows the matching theme panel page, or the hot board when none of those names is on the panel; the heading only ever says 同题材 · <theme> or 平台热门, because that is exactly what the request asked for. Upstream behaviour is backed by a recorded live response in docs/evidence/related-dramas; on-device verification is still open.
- Downloads: choosing episodes no longer enforces a download size quota, so a whole series can be kept offline; a new 同时下载数量 setting (1–5) caps how many transfers run at once instead, and automatic prefetch keeps its own byte budget so manual downloads cannot starve it.
- Manual downloads survive ordinary cache cleanup; resumed tasks keep independent recovery journals.
- Android TV: the episode grid and other nested grids are reachable with the D-pad (Flutter only walked focus inside the scrollable that owned it), and an item that turns inert no longer drops the page into a state with no focus at all. Verified on an emulator with injected remote key events.
- Navigation: pushing a page now slides it in from the right edge and popping walks it back out the same way on every build, replacing the platform defaults that faded forwards on Android and zoomed on Windows/Linux. Verified from recorded frame strips on a macOS window and an iPhone simulator.
- Adaptive immersive player, unified episode/settings panel, auto_route navigation and cached images.
- Application names follow the system language (English, Simplified and Traditional Chinese).
- Only the selected platforms are built in this run; see the platform list below.
- Android APKs, when selected, use the repository's stable release key.
- {tv}
- {ios}
- macOS is ad-hoc signed, not Apple-notarized; Windows is not Authenticode-signed.

GitHub Actions analysis, shared Dart/core/API tests and Flutter widget tests passed before native builds.
Selected platform builds and installer completeness checks passed before publishing.
Device integration tests were not run in this release workflow; local platform validation limits are documented in the repository.
Platforms built in this run: {', '.join(platforms)}.
SHA256SUMS.txt and release-manifest.json describe the attached files.
''')
